  bootwright / render effective
      Show normalized effective desired state. --origins lists, instead of the YAML, where each
      effective field's value came from: authored, defaults.<Kind> (the Environment's kind
      defaults), built-in (a schema default) or derived (normalization). --output-dir writes
      effective-state.yaml into that directory instead of standard output, creating it when it
      is absent, and prints where it wrote; it replaces an earlier file of that name only when
      that is a regular file, and conflicts with --origins. Context-free, --input-dir reads a
      file or directory as validate --file does, requires --output-dir and conflicts with
      --context and --sensitive. Context-backed, --output-dir requires --sensitive, which
      writes mode 0600 under a 0700 directory it creates and refuses an existing output
      directory another account owns or that its group or others can write.

  Usage
    bootwright render effective [flags]

  Command flags
      --input-dir   Read a context-free input file or directory (requires --output-dir)
      --origins     Mark where each effective field's value came from
      --output-dir  Write effective-state.yaml to this directory instead of standard output
      --sensitive   Authorize sensitive artifact materialization

  Common flags
      --ascii       Use ASCII status markers
      --color       Select terminal colors (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --context     Select a context (default: current context)
      --detail      Select human detail (values: compact, full) · default compact
      -h, --help    Show help for this command
      -o, --output  Select output mode (values: text, json, yaml) · default text
      --progress    Select progress animation (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --width       Set presentation width (0: automatic) · default 0

  Examples
    bootwright render effective --input-dir ./input --output-dir ./artifacts
